WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.105
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.629
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:16.041
Unit nine: Describing Graphs and Data. Today you will describe charts, trends and numbers accurately.

4
00:00:16.341 --> 00:00:19.016
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:22.782
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:24.420
Trend.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.310
Trend means a general direction of change.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.301
The trend is upward.

9
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.395
Your turn. Say: Trend.

10
00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:36.956
Trend.

11
00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:38.799
Increase.

12
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.249
Increase means to go up.

13
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.641
Sales increase each year.

14
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.659
Your turn. Say: Increase.

15
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.524
Increase.

16
00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:52.215
Decrease.

17
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:54.868
Decrease means to go down.

18
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:57.262
Prices decrease slowly.

19
00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.514
Your turn. Say: Decrease.

20
00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.623
Decrease.

21
00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:06.384
Fluctuate.

22
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:09.580
Fluctuate means to go up and down.

23
00:01:10.183 --> 00:01:11.858
Prices fluctuate daily.

24
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.079
Your turn. Say: Fluctuate.

25
00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:18.923
Fluctuate.

26
00:01:19.683 --> 00:01:20.661
Proportion.

27
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.615
Proportion means a part of a whole.

28
00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.914
A large proportion agreed.

29
00:01:26.517 --> 00:01:29.065
Your turn. Say: Proportion.

30
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:32.924
Proportion.

31
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:34.336
Peak.

32
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.187
Peak means the highest point.

33
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:39.295
Sales reached a peak.

34
00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:41.978
Your turn. Say: Peak.

35
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:45.486
Peak.

36
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.019
Steady.

37
00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:49.854
Steady means not changing much.

38
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.008
The level stayed steady.

39
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:54.723
Your turn. Say: Steady.

40
00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:58.417
Steady.

41
00:01:59.183 --> 00:02:00.370
Approximately.

42
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:03.093
Approximately means about.

43
00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:06.043
Approximately 40 percent agreed.

44
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.453
Your turn. Say: Approximately.

45
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.545
Approximately.

46
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:18.228
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.269
Visal, how do I describe a graph?

48
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:31.828
Start with a general statement about what the graph shows. Then describe the main trends, give key figures and compare the highest and lowest points.

49
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:34.580
Which verbs do I use?

50
00:02:35.683 --> 00:02:47.110
Use rise, increase and grow for upward change, fall, decrease and drop for downward change, and fluctuate or remain steady for other patterns.

51
00:02:48.217 --> 00:02:50.448
How do I describe speed of change?

52
00:02:51.550 --> 00:03:03.455
Use adverbs such as sharply, gradually and slightly. For example, sales rose sharply in March and then fell slightly in April.

53
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.414
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.770
Grammar focus: Verbs and adverbs of change.

55
00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.315
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:15.167
Sales rose sharply in March.

57
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:18.094
The price fell slightly after that.

58
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:27.177
Use a verb for the direction and an adverb for the speed: rose sharply, fell gradually. Use in or from and to for time and numbers.

59
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:31.266
Be careful! Don't say: Sales rose sharp in March.

60
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.919
Say: Sales rose sharply in March.

61
00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:38.161
Use an adverb after rose.

62
00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:41.352
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.446
A Sales Chart.

64
00:03:43.746 --> 00:03:46.199
The chart shows monthly sales in a small shop.

65
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.047
Sales rose sharply in March and reached a peak.

66
00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:54.194
They fell slightly in April and then stayed steady.

67
00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.337
Approximately forty percent of buyers were students.

68
00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.855
Overall, the trend over the year was upward.

69
00:04:02.967 --> 00:04:06.899
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:09.471
Increase means to go blank.

71
00:04:09.771 --> 00:04:12.751
A, up. B, down. C, away.

72
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.754
The answer is A: up.

73
00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:20.696
Fluctuate means up and blank.

74
00:04:20.996 --> 00:04:24.034
A, over. B, down. C, left.

75
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.216
The answer is B: down.

76
00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:32.199
A peak is the blank point.

77
00:04:32.499 --> 00:04:35.839
A, lowest. B, middle. C, highest.

78
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.469
The answer is C: highest.

79
00:04:42.617 --> 00:04:44.338
Approximately means blank.

80
00:04:44.638 --> 00:04:48.198
A, about. B, never. C, exactly.

81
00:04:51.733 --> 00:04:53.431
The answer is A: about.

82
00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:56.351
What was the overall trend?

83
00:04:56.651 --> 00:05:00.246
A, unknown. B, upward. C, downward.

84
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.556
The answer is B: upward.

85
00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:10.150
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:11.017 --> 00:05:12.633
How do you describe a graph?

87
00:05:21.417 --> 00:05:22.824
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.124 --> 00:05:36.100
I start with a general statement about the graph. Then I describe the main trends with verbs such as rose and fell and adverbs such as sharply. I give key figures and compare the highest and lowest points.

89
00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.156
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.746
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verbs and adverbs of change.

91
00:05:44.046 --> 00:05:48.010
Today's value is precision. Choose your words and numbers with care.

92
00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.672
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:05:50.972 --> 00:05:53.590
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

